  "title": "Indian Corps at Ypres: the 129th Baluchis at Hollebeke",
  "summary": "Indian troops were sent to the Western Front in autumn 1914 to help the exhausted British force, and their first engagement came on 25 October near Ypres. On 31 October the 129th Baluchis, outnumbered about five to one, held Hollebeke; Sepoy Khudadad Khan kept working his gun after being wounded until the rest of his crew were killed.",
